---
/**
 * ONE small example conversation, written for this portfolio. It is not a captured
 * session, contains no real user data, and is labelled as synthetic. The answer is
 * grounded in the published PRIVATE behaviour (integration pack §03).
 */
---

<figure class="sc" role="group" aria-labelledby="sc-label">
  <figcaption class="sc__head">
    <span class="chip chip--prototype" id="sc-label">
      <svg class="chip__glyph" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="5" cy="5" r="3.75" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 1.6" />
      </svg>
      <span class="chip__text">SYNTHETIC DEMO</span>
    </span>
    <span class="sc__note">Example conversation — not a captured session.</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="sc__turn">
    <p class="sc__who">User</p>
    <p class="sc__msg">Explain why PRIVATE mode is fail-closed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="sc__turn sc__turn--yuzuki">
    <p class="sc__who">Yuzuki</p>
    <p class="sc__msg">
      PRIVATE starts only when the selected profile resolves to a loopback provider.
      If validation fails, Yuzuki stops the turn instead of substituting a cloud model.
    </p>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  .sc {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 640px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-panel);
  }

  .sc__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-8) var(--space-12);
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-16);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .sc__note {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
  }

  .sc__turn {
    padding: var(--space-16);
  }

  .sc__turn + .sc__turn {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-soft);
  }

  .sc__who {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .sc__turn--yuzuki .sc__who {
    color: var(--color-violet);
  }

  .sc__msg {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
